// The User-Agent apt announces to every archive it contacts.
//
// It names the distribution and nothing else. What used to stand here was
// /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/01turnkey, written per appliance by mk/turnkey.mk:
//
//   Acquire::http::User-Agent "TurnKey APT-HTTP/1.3 (turnkey-wordpress-19.0-trixie-amd64)";
//
// so deb.debian.org, security.debian.org, every mirror in between and anyone
// watching the connection were told which appliance this machine is and which
// version it runs, on every apt run it ever made. Keel-Linux/common#6.
//
// The https method of apt reads this same setting, so one line covers both.
Acquire::http::User-Agent "Keel APT-HTTP/1.3";
